To the dev team:

   Seems like a bit of a mixup here.  I was under the impression that Cavemen
were big strong apes with the common sense of a gnat.  Heck, I'm even mildly
surprised that they start with a bow and arrows, even, as that seems relatively
post-cro magnon to me.  But anyways, here's something I noticed.  I created ten
random characters of each class, Caveman, Knight and Priest.  And I recorded
all their intelligence scores.  This is what I came up with:

         Caveman        Knight         Priest

#1          10             8              8
#2          11             9              7
#3           9             7             15
#4           8             8              7
#5           8             9             11
#6          10             7             11
#7           9             7             12
#8           9             8              9
#9          10             9             14
#10          9             8             12

Total       93            80            106
Average     9.3           8.0           10.6

   Now, maybe it's just me.  But this seems skewed.  I'd expect Zog the
Troglodyte to average somewhere around 6-7...  Arthur the Knight would 
hover around the 10-11 range, and Jerry Falwell the Priest should be
more consistantly around 13-14.  After all, with the exception of the 
Healer and the Wizard, the Priest should be the most learned of the characters,
right?

